[00:01.42]1. Life, like a mist, appears for just a day,
[00:07.54]Then disappears tomorrow.
[00:15.10]All that we are can quickly fade away,
[00:20.78]Replaced with tears and sorrow.
[00:28.47]If a man should die, can he live again?
[00:34.97]Hear the promise God has made:
[00:40.69](Chorus)
[00:41.15]He will call; The dead will answer.
[00:47.81]They will live at his command.
[00:54.53]For he will have a longing
[01:01.49]For the work of his own hand.
[01:08.77]So have faith, and do not wonder,
[01:15.33]For our God can make us stand.
[01:21.99]And we will live forever,
[01:29.27]As the work of his own hand.
[01:37.31]2. Friends of our God, though they may pass away,
[01:43.37]Will never be forsaken.
[01:51.17]All those asleep who in God’s mem’ry stay,
[01:57.21]From death he will awaken.
[02:04.51]Then we’ll come to see all that life can be:
[02:40.85]Paradise eternally.
[02:44.29](Chorus)
[02:44.55]He will call; The dead will answer.
[02:51.61]They will live at his command.
[02:58.09]For he will have a longing
[03:05.01]For the work of his own hand.
[03:12.27]So have faith, and do not wonder,
[03:19.13]For our God can make us stand.
[03:26.19]And we will live forever,
[03:30.57]As the work of his own hand.
